(c) Brad Smith (rainwarrior), https://rainwarrior.ca
**Licence:** Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International — verified live at
the upstream readme: *"This program was written by Brad Smith. Its source code
is made freely available under the the terms of the Creative Commons
Attribution license: CC BY 4.0"*. https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

| file in this tree | what our copy is |
|---|---|
| `vendor/probe_ref/inc/mode7_diz_ztable.inc` | **verbatim** — the `pv_ztable` reciprocal LUT, 4,096 bytes. Confirmed as `min(255, round(32768 / i))` at all 4,095 non-zero indices, which is the closed form the upstream source documents |
| `vendor/probe_ref/inc/mode7_diz_math.asm` | **modified transliteration** — `umul16`, `smul16`, `smul16_u8`, `udiv32`, `sign`, `sincos` |
| `vendor/probe_ref/src/probe_scene_ref.asm` | **modified transliteration** of `pv_rebuild`, `pv_set_origin`, `pv_abcd_lines_{full,sa1,angle0}`, `pv_interpolate_{2x,4x}`, `pv_buffer_x` — inside an otherwise first-party reference scene |
| `vendor/probes/probe_cpu_ref.asm` | **generated** from the file above by `vendor/probes/make_probe_cpu.py` (7 anchored patches; regeneration verified byte-identical). Carries the same routines |

**Attribution statement:** *This work includes portions of `dizworld.s` by
Brad Smith (rainwarrior), licensed CC BY 4.0. The `pv_ztable`
reciprocal-distance LUT is used unmodified; `pv_rebuild`, `pv_set_origin`,
their supporting math helpers and the per-scanline variant routines are
modified transliterations.*

**Where this reaches a ROM, and where it does not.** These four files are
measurement scaffolding for the CPU calibration probe. They are linked only by
`build/probe_cpu.sfc` and `build/probe_cpu_step.sfc`, which embed the CC BY
code and must carry the credit above. **No `engine/` feature and no `game/`
rail links any of them**, and no asset generator in this repo reads them —
every Mode 7 table this repo ships is computed from closed-form trigonometry
in Python with no third-party file input. The full trace, including the
numeric test that this project's own per-scanline profiles are neither a copy
of nor a resampling of `pv_ztable`, is `docs/92` §4.

Dizworld's own visual assets (OpenGameArt contributions under CC BY 4.0 /
CC BY 3.0, credited in its readme) are **not** present in this repository.

