### Mesen2 — SourMesen and contributors — **GPLv3**

**Upstream:** https://github.com/SourMesen/Mesen2

The emulator is **never committed** — `tools/setup.sh` clones and builds it,
and the repo-local core cache (`tools/Mesen/`) is git-ignored. It is a
development and test tool; it is not linked into, distributed with, or
required by the ROMs this repo produces. Four files nevertheless touch it,
in three groups:

| file in this tree | what it is |
|---|---|
| `vendor/mesen_patches/lockstep_core_edits.patch` | a unified diff against three Mesen2 sources. The added lines are this project's; the **context lines are Mesen2's GPLv3 source** |
| `vendor/mesen_patches/LockstepSync.h`, `LockstepApiWrapper.cpp` | **first-party**, written against Mesen2 headers and compiled into the core. The resulting `MesenCore-lockstep.so` is a **GPLv3 derivative work** and may only be redistributed on GPLv3 terms. It is a build artifact and is not committed |
| `tools/mesen_state_offsets.cpp` | **first-party** — a `printf` program that includes Mesen2 headers to print struct offsets. Not built by the Makefile, not linked, contains no Mesen2 code |

Mesen2's source is additionally read as a **hardware reference** across the
tree (`allocator/schemas.py`, `engine/features/shg_grad/shg_grad.asm` and
others cite it by file and line). Those citations restate hardware behaviour
in this project's own words; no Mesen2 code is reproduced.

